# mutgap4_svc_rate_map_reset_placement_unmappable: ResetRasterizationRateMap (66) while the task's placement list is on a read-only leaf. A mutable rate map (type 7, 256x256, samples {0.25, 1.0}) is made by an info 454 query, which maps (200, 200) to physical coordinates; the guest then writes other samples into its record ({1.0, 0.25}) and moves the lists with SetObjectAndPlacementList (68): the object list where it was, the placement list on VA page 40, read-only. 66 must map both lists first: the object list maps, the placement list needs a writable mapping and does not, so 66 replies 2 and returns with the map untouched: the command faults. With the placement list moved to a writable page (68 again), 454 still maps (200, 200) as before: the new samples were never read. Isolate only (placement lists and 66 are the service's). Keyed by the host: 454's coordinates are Metal's.
